"The most evenly contested fixture of the matchday. CIV Pundit predicts a 2-1 home win, backed by Amad Diallo's momentum from the France scalp and wide attacking quality. ECU Pundit predicts 1-1, arguing Ecuador's defensive organisation (Pacho + Hincapié) neutralises the width threat and the 19-game unbeaten run reflects genuine structural solidity. Both agree this is a genuine 50/50 with the result hinging on whether CIV's attacking width or Ecuador's defensive discipline wins the tactical argument."